    "answer": {
      "short": "$952,\\ 925,\\ 592,\\ 529,\\ 295,\\ 259$",
      "worked": "Use each possible hundreds digit in descending order. For each hundreds digit, place the larger remaining digit in the tens place first.\n\nWith 9 hundreds: $952,\\ 925$.\n\nWith 5 hundreds: $592,\\ 529$.\n\nWith 2 hundreds: $295,\\ 259$.\n\nThere are $3\\times2\\times1=6$ numbers. From largest to smallest:\n\n$952>925>592>529>295>259$.",
